\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af7\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang2057\langfe2052\hich\af4\loch\sl259\slmult1\sb0\sa160\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\ltrpar\cf1\f4\fs24\lang2057\dbch\af7\langfe2052\qj\ltrpar{\loch
The studio opens at nine, and the first hour belongs to whoever arrives with the kettle already filled. Every project begins with a single page that states the problem in plain words, before any sketch is made. Drafts are shared early and often; a rough idea seen by three people is worth more than a polished one seen by none. When a decision is made, it is written down with the date and the reason, so that later we can tell why. Feedback is specific, kind and about the work, never about the person who made it. Each Friday the team tidies the shared drive, archives finished work and leaves a short note for Monday.}
